{{!-- XP and Level, and the Level Up strip they are for. Lives in the rail.

      Not merely a tidy pair: VitalsSnapshot derives XP's ceiling as 6 + level × 2, so Level computes
      XP's max. They are one mechanism, and they are consulted once a session rather than mid-blow —
      which is why they are here and not in the band, and why the rail's own order (the ratings it
      crowns, then the moves) puts them above the move groups.

      The rail is exactly two stat frames wide, so the two sit level and equal. --}}
<div class="stonetop-resource-row stonetop-resource-row--advancement">

	{{!-- `is-full` is the one thing the sheet never said about XP: that the track is at (or past)
	      the Level Up threshold it has been printing all along. It also settles Burn Brightly, which
	      is gated on exactly this and had nothing on screen to read it from. --}}
	<div class="stonetop-vital">
		<div class="stonetop-resource stonetop-resource--wide{{#if stonetop.vitals.readyToLevel}} is-full{{/if}}">
			{{!-- A definition, not provenance: unlike HP/damage/armor, XP has no playbook source to
			      explain, so the hover carries what the book says XP is (Book I, p.53). --}}
			<span class="stonetop-resource__label"
			      data-tooltip="{{localize 'stonetop.character.attributes.desc.xp'}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">{{localize "stonetop.character.attributes.xp"}}</span>
			<div class="stonetop-resource__split">
				<span class="stonetop-stepper">
					<input class="stonetop-resource__input stonetop-char-xp stonetop-step" type="number" data-change-action="xp"
					       aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.xpCurrent'}}"
					       value="{{stonetop.vitals.xp.value}}" min="0">
					{{> "stonetop.stepper-buttons"}}
				</span>
				<span>/</span>
				<span class="stonetop-resource__max">{{stonetop.vitals.xp.max}}</span>
			</div>
		</div>
		{{#if stonetop.vitals.readyToLevel}}
		<span class="stonetop-resource__note stonetop-resource__note--ready">{{localize "stonetop.character.attributes.note.readyToLevel"}}</span>
		{{/if}}
	</div>

	{{!-- No note. Its only candidate — "next at 14" — restates the XP track's own max one tile away,
	      and a note that restates the value beside it is noise. --}}
	<div class="stonetop-vital">
		<div class="stonetop-resource stonetop-resource--wide">
			<span class="stonetop-resource__label">{{localize "stonetop.character.attributes.level"}}</span>
			<span class="stonetop-stepper">
				<input class="stonetop-resource__input stonetop-char-level stonetop-step" type="number" data-change-action="level"
				       aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.character.attributes.level'}}"
				       value="{{stonetop.vitals.level}}" min="1">
				{{> "stonetop.stepper-buttons"}}
			</span>
		</div>
	</div>

</div>

{{!-- Directly under the XP track it is about, not hanging after the numbers: levelling up is what
      XP and Level are FOR, and the move that does it spends the one and raises the other. Renders
      nothing at all unless it has triggered or left something outstanding, which is most of the
      time. --}}
{{> "stonetop.level-up-strip"}}
